# AXIS CELL: consumer = the `SIf` DIVERGENCE twin — the `has_unconditional_else`
# accumulator inlined in `live_stmt_diverges`'s `SIf` arm
# (self_host_typechecker/typecheck.gg). That is a FOURTH consumer of the
# fall-through question, distinct from the three `safety_commit` JOIN consumers
# of `elsebranches_have_uncond`.
#
# ⚠ `if_no_else_join_use_after_move_reject.gg` CANNOT see this one. Its `if`
# body does not diverge, so `live_stmt_diverges` returns at the first check and
# never reaches the accumulator's tail; it watches the JOIN consumer. This cell
# watches the DIVERGENCE consumer. Same predicate family, different consumer —
# and a per-consumer weakening is invisible to every cell but its own.
#
# The inner `if a: / elif b:` chain has every branch `return`, but there is NO
# unconditional `else`, so control can reach the end of the outer `if` body with
# `s` still moved. `print(s)` is then a use-after-move, and `gg check` rejects it
# with `error[E_UseAfterMove]`.
#
# RED-VERIFY (weaken the twin's tail): in `live_stmt_diverges`'s `SIf` arm change
# `return has_unconditional_else` to `return true` and rebuild the driver.
# Measured: this cell flips rc 1 -> rc 0, 4046 bytes of C, and it is the ONLY
# outcome cell that moves — the sibling JOIN cell, every match cell, both accept
# canaries and all eleven pre-existing driver cells stay GREEN.
void sink(String ^x):
    pass

void probe(bool a, bool b, bool c):
    String s = "hello"
    if c:
        sink(^s)
        if a:
            return
        elif b:
            return
    print(s)

void main():
    probe(false, false, true)
